 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” lawyer for every Houston car wreck. Based on the available listings, **Joshua P. Davis** is one strong candidate to interview: his profile says he is board-certified in Personal Injury Trial Law by the Texas Board of Legal Specialization, handles car and motor-vehicle cases, and has been selected to Super Lawyers from 2021–2026. **Kevin M. Camp** is another Houston option with board certification and a practice that includes automobile accidents.\n\nBefore hiring anyone, speak with two or three lawyers and ask:\n- Who will personally handle my case?\n- How often do you take car-wreck cases like mine to trial?\n- What is the contingency fee, and what case costs might I owe?\n- What is your assessment of liability, insurance coverage, and likely next steps?\n\nYou can also get a Houston-area referral through the **Houston Lawyer Referral Service** at **(800) 289-4577**. This is a starting point, not a guarantee of fit; verify the lawyer’s current license and disciplinary history with the State Bar of Texas.",
